## 32. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The application is not complete until the following requirements are met.

### Authentication
- Users can sign in and sign out.
- Password recovery works.
- Public registration cannot grant privileged roles.
- Protected pages require authentication.

### Permissions
- Users only access records they are authorized to see.
- Students cannot modify official marks or attendance.
- Parents cannot view unrelated students' records.
- Teachers cannot manage unrelated classes.
- Private conversations are accessible only to participants.
- Discussion groups enforce membership permissions.

### Academic functionality
- Administrators can manage authorized classes and subjects.
- Teachers can create assignments.
- Students can submit files.
- Teachers can grade submissions.
- Marks are persisted.
- Report cards use actual saved records.
- Attendance is persisted and validated.
- Announcements reach the intended audience.

### Communication
- Private messages persist.
- Authorized users can access conversations.
- Discussion posts and replies persist.
- Notifications link to relevant content.
- Moderation permissions work.

### Gemini AI
- The application uses the configured Google Gemini model.
- AI requests run through a secure backend.
- Quiz generation produces validated question data.
- Grading suggestions require teacher approval.
- Tutor conversations are saved.
- Performance insights use authorized records.
- AI failures are handled gracefully.

### User experience
- The application is responsive.
- Navigation is consistent.
- Forms validate input.
- Loading and error states are visible.
- Buttons perform their intended actions.
- No critical feature is represented solely by placeholder content.

